// Scene: Scavenger Origin — Opening
// You and Isolde arrive in Grima, the blighted village on Aren Island.
// Establishes: the job, Isolde's guarded personality, Orin's disappearance, the artifact.

With a soft <em>thunk</em>, the Skyship <em>Intrepid</em> makes an impressive landing near the edge of the blighted township.

The land around looks just like what you expected: a desolate, gray wasteland. Just like the rest of the Sundered Lands. Rooftops caved in, docks rotting in the water... Nothing moves except the odd piece of cloth buffeted by the wind.

* [Head to the gangway]
    -> gangway




=== gangway ===
Isolde is already at the gangway when you reach it.

She turns to you. "Stay close until we know what we're dealing with."

* ["You've been here before?"]
    She shakes her head. "Grima? It's a sundered town. I've read everything my father wrote about it. I know what it was."
    She doesn't say what it is <em>now</em>. What it's become.
    -> arrival

* [Step off the gangway first.]
    She lets you. Whether it's trust or pragmatism, you can't tell.
    -> arrival




=== arrival ===
As you step off the gangway, you're hit by the sour smell of decay. Isolde begins to cough violently before covering her mouth and nose with a breathing cloth.

* [Walk into town]
    -> streets

=== streets ===

You move through the first street together. Abandoned carts. A well with the rope cut. Doors hanging open. Everywhere, the purple-gray ooze of blightrot lingers in the shadows.

Grima is quiet in the way that feels like something is listening.

* ["Tell me about your father."]
    "<em>Orin von Solveig</em>. Merchant. Explorer. Stubborn to the point of embarrassment."
    She pauses and adjusts the cloth over her nose.
    "He came to Aren six weeks ago chasing rumors of a pre-Cataclysm artifact. He sent one letter from Freehaven and then... nothing."
    -> the_job

* ["What are we <em>actually</em> looking for?"]
    "My father, first. Or whatever remains of him."
    Her voice doesn't waver. She's had time to prepare for that sentence.
    "And that artifact he was after. I don't know what it does, but I know it's important. I know that's why he came here, why he left us."
    -> the_job

* [Say nothing. Keep scanning the rooftops.]
    She notices. She approves, maybe.
    -> the_job




=== the_job ===
"You were recommended to me in Freehaven as someone who knows how to navigate places like this. That's why you're here."

* ["What does the artifact do?"]
    Isolde shrugs. "I don't know. My father's notes are... incomplete. He was careful about what he committed to paper."
    She absentmindedly touches the satchel that hangs by her side.
    "I'm still working through them."
    -> closing

* ["And if someone else is looking for it?"]
    "Then we find it first."
    Short. Final. She's already considered this.
    -> closing

* ["Understood. What do you need from me now?"]
    She turns to you. "Your eyes and your experience. I can handle the research. I can't handle..."
    She gestures broadly at the collapsed building to your left.
    "This."
    -> closing




=== closing ===
Somewhere deeper in the village, something shifts. A sound too heavy for wind.

Isolde shoulders her satchel. "We should keep moving."

She draws her coat tight and walks forward without waiting for you.

-> END
